      "fullAnswer": "### 1. Forest Resources\nForest resources encompass global forest ecosystems covering nearly 31% of Earth's land surface. Forests provide critical ecological services including oxygen production, carbon dioxide sequestration, climate regulation, soil erosion prevention, watershed maintenance, habitat for 80% of terrestrial biodiversity, and commercial timber, fuelwood, and medicinal herbs.\n\n### 2. Major Causes of Deforestation\n1. **Agricultural Expansion:** Clearing tropical rainforests for commercial cattle ranching, soybean cultivation, and palm oil plantations.\n2. **Commercial Logging & Fuelwood:** Indiscriminate timber extraction for building construction, paper pulp production, and fuelwood gathering.\n3. **Infrastructure & Mining Operations:** Constructing highways, hydroelectric mega-dams, urban housing, and open-pit mineral mining operations.\n4. **Forest Fires & Climate Change:** Severe forest wildfires exacerbated by global warming and prolonged droughts.\n\n### 3. Severe Environmental Effects of Deforestation\n1. **Loss of Biodiversity & Species Extinction:** Destruction of natural habitats driving thousands of tropical flora and fauna species to extinction.\n2. **Accelerated Climate Change & Global Warming:** Burning and felling trees releases stored carbon dioxide into the atmosphere, aggravating the greenhouse effect.\n3. **Soil Erosion & Desertification:** Removal of root systems leads to topsoil wash-away during rains, decreasing soil fertility and causing land degradation.\n4. **Disruption of the Hydrological Water Cycle:** Loss of plant transpiration reduces atmospheric humidity, causing lower regional rainfall and frequent severe droughts.\n\n### 4. Conservation Measures\nEnforcing strict anti-logging laws, promoting global afforestation programs, and establishing protected biological corridors.",
