      "fullAnswer": "### 1. Concept of the CSS Box Model\nEvery HTML element rendered in a web browser is treated as a rectangular box. The CSS Box Model dictates the layout and total dimensions (width and height) of elements.\n\n### 2. Four Concentric Layers of the Box Model\n1. **Content Box:** The innermost area where actual text, images, or video elements appear. Width and height properties set content dimensions.\n2. **Padding:** Transparent spacing layer surrounding content inside the element's border (`padding-top`, `padding-right`, etc.).\n3. **Border:** Line or frame surrounding padding and content (`border: 2px solid blue`).\n4. **Margin:** Transparent spacing outside the border separating the element from neighboring elements.\n\n### 3. Total Dimension Formula\n$$\text{Total Width} = \text{Width} + \text{Padding (Left + Right)} + \text{Border (Left + Right)} + \text{Margin (Left + Right)}$$\n\n### 4. `box-sizing: border-box` Property\nSetting `box-sizing: border-box` includes padding and border inside the declared width, preventing layout breakage.",
