      "fullAnswer": "### 1. Definition of Affixes\nAffixes are morphemes added to root words to alter their meaning, tense, or grammatical word class.\n\n### 2. Types of Affixes\n- **Prefixes (Added before root word):** Modify the meaning of the root word.\n  - *un-* + *happy* = *unhappy* (negation)\n  - *re-* + *write* = *rewrite* (repetition)\n  - *micro-* + *processor* = *microprocessor* (size)\n- **Suffixes (Added after root word):** Change the part of speech or grammatical class.\n  - *quick* (adj) + *-ly* = *quickly* (adv)\n  - *develop* (verb) + *-ment* = *development* (noun)\n  - *program* (noun) + *-mer* = *programmer* (noun agent)\n\n### 3. Importance in Technical Communication\nAffixes enable technical professionals to construct precise jargon-free terms, expand vocabulary efficiency, and understand unfamiliar domain terminology.",
      "quickMemory": "AFFIXES IN VOCABULARY (5 MARKS)\nPREFIXES (Before root): un- + happy = unhappy, re- + write = rewrite\nSUFFIXES (After root): quick + -ly = quickly, develop + -ment = development",
