      "fullAnswer": "### 1. Keyboard Definition & Overview\nA keyboard is the primary alphanumeric input peripheral device used to enter text, numeric data, system commands, and control signals into a computer system.\n\n### 2. Key Functions & Key Layout Breakdown\n1. **Alphanumeric Keys:** Letters (A-Z) and numbers (0-9) used for text entry and word processing.\n2. **Function Keys (F1-F12):** Dedicated shortcut keys performing specific operating system and application actions (e.g., F1 for Help, F5 for Refresh).\n3. **Control & Modifier Keys:** Ctrl, Alt, Shift, and Windows keys used in combination with other keys to execute software shortcuts.\n4. **Navigation Keys:** Arrow keys, Home, End, Page Up, and Page Down for cursor positioning in documents.\n5. **Key Matrix Matrix Encoding:** Internal micro-controller scans key matrix circuits, converting physical keystrokes into binary ASCII/Unicode scan codes sent to CPU interrupts.\n\n### 3. Conclusion\nKeyboards remain the indispensable text input interface for computer programming and administrative data entry.",
