      "fullAnswer": "### 1. Overview of HTTP Status Codes\nHTTP status codes are 3-digit numerical response codes issued by a web server in response to a client's HTTP request. They indicate whether a specific HTTP request succeeded, redirected, or encountered an error.\n\n### 2. Major HTTP Status Code Categories\n1. **2xx Success:**\n   - **`200 OK`:** Standard successful HTTP response. Server successfully retrieved or processed requested web resource.\n   - **`201 Created`:** Request succeeded and a new backend resource was created (via HTTP POST).\n2. **3xx Redirection:**\n   - **`301 Moved Permanently`:** Requested URL resource has been permanently moved to a new URI location.\n3. **4xx Client Error:**\n   - **`400 Bad Request`:** Server cannot process request due to malformed client syntax.\n   - **`404 Not Found`:** Server cannot find requested webpage or asset.\n4. **5xx Server Error:**\n   - **`500 Internal Server Error`:** Generic error message when an unexpected server-side code exception occurs.\n\n### 3. Conclusion\nHTTP status codes are crucial for web developer debugging, REST API client communication, and web search engine indexing.",
