      "fullAnswer": "### 1. What is a Web Cookie?\nA HTTP cookie is a small text data file (up to 4KB) sent by web servers and stored in client web browsers to maintain session state across stateless HTTP requests.\n\n### 2. Setting Cookies in JavaScript\nCookies are set using the `document.cookie` property by assigning key-value pairs along with optional `expires`, `max-age`, `path`, and `SameSite` attributes.\n```js\n// Setting a cookie expiring in 7 days\ndocument.cookie = \"username=Nadeer; max-age=604800; path=/; SameSite=Lax\";\n```\n\n### 3. Retrieving Cookies in JavaScript\nRetrieving `document.cookie` returns a semicolon-separated string of all active cookies for the current domain.\n```js\n// Retrieving and parsing cookie string\nfunction getCookie(name) {\n    let cookies = document.cookie.split('; ');\n    for (let c of cookies) {\n        let [key, val] = c.split('=');\n        if (key === name) return val;\n    }\n    return null;\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Conclusion\nCookies enable user login persistence, shopping cart state retention, and web analytics tracking.",
